Run Snort in Packet Sniffing Mode
bash
Copy
Edit
sudo snort -i eth0 -A console -q -c /etc/snort/snort.conf
-i: interface to listen on

-A console: alert mode to console

-q: quiet (less output)

-c: config file path

Replace eth0 with your actual interface.

Create a Simple Rule
Create a local rules file:

bash
Copy
Edit
sudo nano /etc/snort/rules/local.rules
Add this rule (detects ping):

snort
Copy
Edit
alert icmp any any -> any any (msg:"ICMP Packet Detected"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
Edit the main config file to include your rule:

bash
Copy
Edit
sudo nano /etc/snort/snort.conf
Find the line:

bash
Copy
Edit
include $RULE_PATH/local.rules
Make sure it's uncommented.
 Test the Rule
Start Snort:

bash
Copy
Edit
sudo snort -A console -q -i eth0 -c /etc/snort/snort.conf
In another terminal, run a ping:

bash
Copy
Edit
ping -c 1 8.8.8.8
Snort should detect it and print:

css
Copy
Edit
[**] [1:1000001:1] ICMP Packet Detected [**]
